The re-run is what [[rerun_requests]] is for, so it must survive the fix.
A service provider redirects an unauthenticated request to the identity
provider; once [[SAMLlogin]] has relayed the assertion, the same request
succeeds.
<<test functions>>=
def test_SAMLlogin_reruns_the_original_request_after_the_relay():
  logged_in = []

  def api(request):
    if logged_in:
      return 200, {}, "data"
    return 302, {"Location": IDP_REDIRECT_SSO + "?execution=e1s1"}, ""

  def acs(request):
    logged_in.append(True)
    return 200, {}, "logged in"

  services = FakeServices({
    ("GET", f"{SP}/api"): api,
    ("GET", IDP_REDIRECT_SSO): lambda r: (200, {}, relay_form(f"{SP}/acs")),
    ("POST", f"{SP}/acs"): acs,
  })
  session = session_with(
    services, weblogin.kth.SAMLlogin(rerun_requests=True))

  response = session.get(f"{SP}/api")

  assert response.text == "data"
  assert services.count("GET", f"{SP}/api") == 2
@

A service provider that never accepts the assertion sends the re-run back to
the identity provider.
We relay that second round too, but we do not re-run again: the request would
only take the same round once more.
