A handler that has re-run a request must still equal a fresh one with the same
configuration.
Programs that share a session add their handlers with [[add_handler]], which
skips a handler that is already present by comparing them
(\cref{HandlerEquality}); [[kthutils]] adds its [[SAMLlogin]] to [[ladok3]]'s
cached session on every run.
If the flag of the third rule counted as configuration, every such run would
add one more [[SAMLlogin]], and each copy would repeat the request once more.
<<test functions>>=
def test_SAMLlogin_is_not_duplicated_after_a_rerun():
  services = FakeServices({
    ("GET", f"{SP}/api"):
      lambda r: (302, {"Location": IDP_REDIRECT_SSO + "?execution=e1s1"}, ""),
    ("GET", IDP_REDIRECT_SSO): lambda r: (200, {}, relay_form(f"{SP}/acs")),
    ("POST", f"{SP}/acs"): lambda r: (200, {}, "ok"),
  })
  session = session_with(
    services, weblogin.kth.SAMLlogin(rerun_requests=True))
  session.get(f"{SP}/api")

  session.add_handler(weblogin.kth.SAMLlogin(rerun_requests=True))

  assert len(session._AutologinSession__handlers) == 1
